                <pb facs="0348" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg288"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>French ambassador here cables his Government to-day in favor of Waller’s release
                    because of his ill health and on grounds of humanity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
